-- title:
--   No nonzero homomorphism from a finite-height formal group to Gₐ
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field of characteristic $p$, with $p$ prime, and let $F_0$ be an $n$-dimensional commutative-style formal group law over $k$ in the sense of the project's structure [`MvFormalGroup`](def/MvFormalGroup_BasicV2.html#L15): a tuple of $n$ power series $F_0^{(i)} \in k[[X_1,\dots,X_n,Y_1,\dots,Y_n]]$ (the two groups of variables indexed by the two summands of `Fin n ⊕ Fin n`) each with zero constant term, with the coefficient of $X_j$ in $F_0^{(i)}$ and the coefficient of $Y_j$ in $F_0^{(i)}$ both equal to $\delta_{ij}$, and satisfying associativity $F_0(F_0(X,Y),Z) = F_0(X,F_0(Y,Z))$ as an identity of substitutions in $3n$ variables. Write $F_0.\mathrm{nthSeries}$ for the iterated multiplication series, defined by $[0] = 0$ and $[m+1]^{(i)} = F_0^{(i)}([m](X),X)$. Assume there is a natural number $h$ with $\dim_k\big(k[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]/([p](X)_1,\dots,[p](X)_n)\big) = p^h$, the ideal being generated by the components of $[p]$. Let $f \in k[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]$ have zero constant term and satisfy $f(F_0(X,Y)) - f(X) - f(Y) = 0$, i.e. the additive coboundary `addCoboundary` of $f$ vanishes. Then $f = 0$.
--
--   This is the classical statement that a formal group law of finite height over a field of characteristic $p$ admits no nonzero homomorphism to the additive formal group $\mathbb{G}_a$, with finiteness of height expressed as the condition that the quotient of the power series ring by the ideal generated by the components of the multiplication-by-$p$ series has $k$-dimension $p^h$. It is used in the construction of symmetric two-cocycles attached to such formal groups and, in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting, in the analysis of coboundaries for special formal $O_D$-modules.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvFormalGroup_eq_zero_of_addCoboundary_eq_zero_of_finrank_quotient_span_nthSeries_eq_pow.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_MvFormalGroup_TwoCocycle

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

theorem MvFormalGroup.eq_zero_of_addCoboundary_eq_zero_of_finrank_quotient_span_nthSeries_eq_pow
    {k : Type u} [Field k] (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] [CharP k p]
    {n : ℕ} (F₀ : MvFormalGroup n k) (h : ℕ)
    (hh : Module.finrank k (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k ⧸
      Ideal.span (Set.range (F₀.nthSeries p))) = p ^ h)
    (f : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k) (hf0 : MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff f = 0)
    (hf : F₀.addCoboundary f = 0) : f = 0 := by sorry
